  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{7}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{7})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{7}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{7})=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{6\\pi }{7}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
